    {
      "id": "claim_efb59cab6166450aaf6cbd3065ceb174",
      "statement": "Model retry wraps only the model node, avoiding replay of completed tool calls; it owns transient-error classification, backoff, and visible retry status, while the clients consume attempt and retry events to reconcile partial output.",
